TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

$a = random(2,15,1);
$b = random(2,15,1);
while ($a == $b) { $b = random(2,15,1); }

BEGIN_TEXT
Compute the matrix of the linear operator \(T\) on \(\operatorname{M}_{2\times 2}({\mathbb R})\) defined by the formula \(T(A)=$a A + $b A^T\),
relative to the standard basis of \(\operatorname{M}_{2\times 2}({\mathbb R})\text{.}\)
$PAR
\([T]_S = \) \{ answer_matrix(4,4,5) \} 

END_TEXT

$c = $a+$b;

ANS(num_cmp($c));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp($a));
ANS(num_cmp($b));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp($b));
ANS(num_cmp($a));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp(0));
ANS(num_cmp($a+$b));


